[Graphics:Bonuses]
The game does not give these sprites a colour of their own. They are drawn in the white ink of the playing area, so they are shown here in white.
#UDGTABLE(default,centre,centre,centre,centre,centre,centre,centre,centre)
  { #N$02 | #SPRITE$02,attr=$47(speed-bonus-colour*) | #N$03 | #SPRITE$03,attr=$47(health-bonus-colour*) }
UDGTABLE#

[Graphics:Items]
The game colours the items in the same way as the monsters that need them, which are bright red, magenta, green and cyan for the items #N$01 to #N$04.
#UDGTABLE(default,centre,centre,centre,centre,centre,centre,centre,centre)
  { #N$04, #N$08 | #SPRITE$04,attr=$42(item-1-colour*) | #N$05, #N$09 | #SPRITE$05,attr=$43(item-2-colour*) | #N$06, #N$0A | #SPRITE$06,attr=$44(item-3-colour*) | #N$07, #N$0B | #SPRITE$07,attr=$45(item-4-colour*) }
UDGTABLE#

